## Key terms (security control — L4)

| Term | Description |
|------|-------------|
| Access control | User and group permissions, roles, and least-privilege principle applied to files, shares, and applications. The administrator defines who can read, write, or execute; reviews permissions periodically; and removes access when no longer required. Misconfiguration can lead to data exposure or denial of service. |
| Authentication | Passwords, multi-factor authentication (MFA), certificates, and single sign-on (SSO) as per organisational policy. Strong authentication reduces risk of unauthorised access. The administrator configures password policy, MFA enrolment, and SSO integration and documents the authentication flow. |
| Firewall and network security | Firewall rules (allow/deny by port, protocol, source, and destination), network segmentation (e.g. VLANs), and intrusion detection or prevention (IDS/IPS) where applicable. Rules must be documented and reviewed periodically; overly permissive rules increase risk. |
| Patching | Operating system and application security updates; testing in a non-production environment before rollout; scheduling reboots and change windows; recording applied patches in a change log. Unpatched systems are vulnerable to known exploits. |

